<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal net forex reserves down $480 mln in June.</title>
<headline>Portugal net forex reserves down $480 mln in June.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Portugal's net foreign exchange reserves, including gold valued at market prices, fell by $480 million to $19.29 billion in June, the central bank said in its latest monthly review of the economy.</p>
<p>Figures in dollars:-</p>
<p>					  June 1997     Jan-June 1997</p>
<p> Change in reserves		 -480 million	 -375 million</p>
<p> Total net forex reserves	 19.287 bln	 -</p>
<p>-- Lisbon newsroom +(351-1) 3538254</p>
